    citation: {
      url: "https://doi.org/10.1145/3591221",
      title: "Mostly Automated Proof Repair for Verified Libraries",
      venue: "Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages",
      year: 2023,
    },
    brief: { zh: "从示例补丁归纳 proof-term 变换、沿类型等价迁移函数与证明、为规范不变但实现演化的库自动推断新不变量，并逐类报告自动转换覆盖率、失败证明与人工补丁量。", en: "Induce proof-term transformations from example patches, migrate functions and proofs along type equivalences, infer new invariants for libraries whose specification holds but whose implementation evolves — and report, per change class, automatic conversion coverage, failed proofs and the volume of manual patching." },
    literature: [
      { title: "Proof repair across type equivalences", venue: "Proceedings of the 42nd ACM SIGPLAN International Conference on Programming Language Design and Implementation", year: 2021, url: "https://doi.org/10.1145/3453483.3454033" },
      { title: "Adapting proof automation to adapt proofs", venue: "Proceedings of the 7th ACM SIGPLAN International Conference on Certified Programs and Proofs", year: 2018, url: "https://doi.org/10.1145/3176245.3167094" },
    ],
    depth: {
      overview: { zh: "形式化库的真正成本不在首次证明，而在定义一改、下游成千条证明全断。PUMPKIN PATCH 从示例补丁归纳 proof-term 变换并用于 Coq 标准库更新；PUMPKIN Pi 在八个案例中跨类型等价迁移函数与证明；后续工作又为规范不变、实现演化的已验证库自动推断新不变量。", en: "The real cost of a formal library is not the first proof but the thousands of downstream proofs that break when one definition changes. PUMPKIN PATCH induces proof-term transformations from example patches and applies them to Coq standard-library updates; PUMPKIN Pi migrates functions and proofs across type equivalences in eight case studies; later work infers new invariants for verified libraries whose specification is fixed while the implementation evolves." },
      whyMatters: { zh: "大型形式化库的可持续性取决于重构成本能否被摊平；但工具修好了证明并不说明新定义还表达原意，修复结果必须重新过一遍小内核检查。", en: "The sustainability of a large formal library depends on whether refactoring cost can be amortized. But a tool making the proofs pass again does not show the new definition still means what the old one meant, and every repaired result must go back through the small trusted kernel." },
      ifAnswered: { zh: "重构不再依赖维护者的个人英雄主义：定义演进有了可报告的覆盖率，大型形式化库才可能在多人协作下持续生长。", en: "Refactoring would stop depending on a maintainer's personal heroics: definition evolution would carry a reportable coverage figure, and only then can a large formal library keep growing under many hands." },
      approaches: [
        { zh: "从人工补丁样本归纳 proof-term 层面的变换，再把它回放到标准库中同类断裂的证明上。", en: "Induce proof-term-level transformations from samples of manual patches, then replay them onto standard-library proofs broken in the same way." },
        { zh: "把新旧定义之间的类型等价显式写出，再沿这条等价自动搬运受影响的函数与全部证明。", en: "Write out the type equivalence between old and new definitions explicitly, then transport the affected functions and all their proofs along it automatically." },
        { zh: "对规范不变、实现被改写的验证库，自动搜索并重建足以重新闭合证明的新不变量。", en: "For verified libraries whose specification is unchanged but whose implementation is rewritten, search for and rebuild the new invariants sufficient to close the proofs again." },
      ],
      barrier: { zh: "修复只保证证明重新通过，不保证新定义还在说同一件事；破坏性规范变更没有等价可依，而现有证据几乎全落在 Coq/Rocq 的受控演化案例里。", en: "Repair guarantees only that proofs pass again, not that the new definition still says the same thing. Breaking specification changes offer no equivalence to transport along, and nearly all existing evidence sits inside controlled evolution cases in Coq/Rocq." },
      subQuestions: [
        { zh: "哪些变化类别（重命名、类型等价、规范收紧）存在可判定的自动迁移，哪些必然需要人工？", en: "Which classes of change — renaming, type equivalence, tightened specification — admit decidable automatic migration, and which necessarily require human work?" },
        { zh: "修复后的库要额外承担什么证明义务，才能说明新定义在使用侧与旧定义确实等价？", en: "What additional proof obligation must a repaired library discharge to show that the new definition really is equivalent to the old one from the client's side?" },
        { zh: "跨证明助手迁移时，从 Coq/Rocq 归纳出的 proof-term 变换还剩多少可移植性？", en: "Migrating across proof assistants, how much portability remains in proof-term transformations induced from Coq/Rocq?" },
      ],
    },
